This project implements an 11-stage agentic code review protocol for OpenCode,
derived from the Sashiko project's review architecture.

================================================================================

This project includes material derived from the following projects:

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Sashiko - Agentic review of Linux Kernel code changes
Copyright The Linux Foundation and its contributors. All rights reserved.
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
https://github.com/sashiko-dev/sashiko

The 11-stage review protocol (stage prompt structure, stage sequencing,
concern/dismissed-concern JSON schema, deduplication and conflict resolution
logic, severity calibration guide, and report generation format) is derived
from Sashiko's review pipeline as implemented in src/worker/prompts.rs and
src/worker/stage.rs of the Sashiko project.

The file prompts/severity.md is reproduced from
third_party/prompts/kernel/severity.md in the Sashiko project.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
review-prompts - AI review prompts for Linux kernel development
Copyright (c) 2025 Chris Mason
Licensed under the MIT License
https://github.com/masoncl/review-prompts

Included as a Git submodule at third_party/review-prompts. These prompts
provide per-subsystem and generic kernel review knowledge including
technical-patterns.md, callstack.md, false-positive-guide.md,
inline-template.md, and subsystem-specific guides.

The generic review guides in prompts/ (technical-patterns-generic.md,
callstack-generic.md, false-positive-guide-generic.md, and
inline-template-generic.md) are derived from the kernel-specific
originals in the review-prompts project.
